                                    "text": "An audio-rate modulator makes new tones. The source is a sine so the spectroscope~ reads clearly: Ring 0 = AM, three peaks (the source plus a tone either side); Ring 1 = ring mod, the source peak cancels and only the sum and difference tones remain. Left: turn Ring on the dials. Right: the plain object with a slow LFO on Ring, morphing AM <-> ring mod by itself."
